organisationCode.description:
Property. Four alpha-numeric code allocated by ERA to a body. It represents the Infrastructure Manager (IM) code in RINF.
Infrastructure manager means any body or firm responsible in particular for establishing, managing and maintaining railway infrastructure, including traffic management and control-command signalling; 
the functions of the infrastructure manager on a network or part of a network may be allocated to different bodies or firms. Definition in (Article 3(2)) (RINF register parameter index: 1.1.0.0.0.1, 1.1.1.1.8.1, 1.2.1.0.0.1, 1.2.1.0.5.1, 1.2.1.0.6.1, 1.2.2.0.0.1, 1.2.2.0.5.1)
